## 17. Development workflow — mandatory

Work in incremental, verifiable phases.

### Phase 0 — Repository inspection
Inspect existing files, dependencies, scripts, environment configuration, and project state. Report what already works and what is missing. Do not overwrite existing working code without reason.

### Phase 1 — Foundation and design system
Build the responsive shell, typography, color system, navigation, footer, logo, accessible components, and page routing.

### Phase 2 — Homepage and 3D experience
Implement the 3D awareness ribbon, homepage hero, Anime.js animations, reduced-motion mode, responsive fallback, and performance controls.

### Phase 3 — Education pages
Build content pages, article models, source references, and the medical-review workflow.

### Phase 4 — Secure backend
Implement database connection, authentication, authorization, validation, rate limiting, audit logging, and security tests.

### Phase 5 — Nationwide facility finder
Build facility ingestion, deduplication, geospatial indexing, map interface, nearby search, city search, verification badges, and correction reports.

### Phase 6 — Educational AI assistant
Implement retrieval from approved content, citations, safe response behavior, provider configuration, and abuse protection.

### Phase 7 — Urdu, accessibility, and SEO
Implement RTL support, translation review, accessibility improvements, and crawlable metadata.

### Phase 8 — Testing and deployment
Run tests, fix defects, document configuration, and verify the production build.

At the end of every phase:
1. Summarize what was implemented.
2. List files created or modified.
3. Report commands actually run and their results.
4. Identify incomplete work and blockers.
5. Fix broken imports, routes, API calls, and build errors before proceeding.
6. Do not replace functional code with placeholders to make the task appear complete.
7. Keep a concise progress checklist in `docs/PROGRESS.md`.

